-- Sale of Goods Act 1979 (Singapore; the Act applied from England), 2020 Revised Edition,
-- informal consolidation in force from 1/4/2022.  LAYER 1, NOUNS: the shared words.
-- Only DECLARE here: no rule, no #EVAL.  Every other soga- module imports this one.
-- Membership test (Guide, step 4): a witness of ordinary competence could testify to the fact.
-- Every constructor name below is unique across the whole encoding (work/dups.py checks that).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- The two parties to a contract of sale (s 2(1): "the seller" and "the buyer").
DECLARE `Party to the sale` IS ONE OF
    Seller
    Buyer

-- The parties who may be named as performers of an act in a regulative rule (ss 27, 32, 34, 46, 57).
DECLARE `Person named in the Act` IS ONE OF
    `the seller`
    `the buyer`
    `the carrier or other bailee or custodier`
    `the auctioneer`

-- s 2(4) and (5): what a contract of sale is called.
DECLARE `Stage of the contract` IS ONE OF
    `a sale`
    `an agreement to sell`

-- s 2(3): "A contract of sale may be absolute or conditional."
DECLARE `Absolute or conditional` IS ONE OF
    `an absolute contract`
    `a conditional contract`

-- s 11(2) and s 61(1) "warranty": a stipulation is a condition or a warranty.
DECLARE `Kind of stipulation` IS ONE OF
    `a condition`
    `a warranty`

-- s 11(2): what the contract calls a stipulation (the label does not decide it).
DECLARE `Label the contract gives a stipulation` IS ONE OF
    `the contract calls it a condition`
    `the contract calls it a warranty`
    `the contract gives it no label`

-- s 11(2): how the contract is construed on the stipulation (outside the text).
DECLARE `Construction of a stipulation` IS ONE OF
    `construed as a condition`
    `construed as a warranty`
    `not yet construed`

-- s 4(1): how a contract of sale may be made.
DECLARE `Form of the contract of sale` IS ONE OF
    `made in writing`
    `made by word of mouth`
    `made partly in writing and partly by word of mouth`
    `implied from the conduct of the parties`
    `made in some other form`

-- s 14(2B): the aspects of the quality of goods that the subsection names.
DECLARE `Aspect of the quality of goods` IS ONE OF
    `the state and condition of the goods`
    `fitness for all the purposes for which goods of the kind are commonly supplied`
    `appearance and finish`
    `freedom from minor defects`
    `safety`
    `durability`
    `some other aspect`
